  urldate = {2024-06-06},
  abstract = {How people consume information is evolving. So is JAMA Medical News. This issue debuts JAMA Data Brief, a new department in the journal's long-standing Medical News \&amp; Perspectives.Each JAMA Data Brief will include multiple data visualizations crafted by the journal's Editorial Graphics team on a specific topic. Written by journalists---or in some cases the researchers behind the featured data---the stories accompanying these visual elements will contextualize the numbers and other data points within the broader perspectives of health, health care, and health policy. The news team will be on the lookout for datasets that are timely, newsworthy, and topical to clinical, research, and public health audiences. These data-driven, graphic-rich stories will be concise and readily viewed on multiple devices, including cell phones.},
