  urldate = {2022-06-26},
  abstract = {Recently, apprehension has been raised regarding ``A1/A2 hypothesis'' suggesting relationship between consumption of A1 ``like'' variants of cow {$\beta$}-casein and various physiological disorders. The information available is based on either the human epidemiological data of milk consumption or in vitro trials on cell lines with {$\beta$}-casomorphin peptides. The direct scientific evidence establishing the link between consumption of A1/A2 ``like'' milk and health is scanty. Thus, under present investigation, in vivo trials in mice were undertaken to study the effect of feeding three genetic variants (A1A1, A1A2 and A2A2) of cow {$\beta$}-casein milk on gastrointestinal immune system as it is the first and foremost site of immunological interactions.},
