  urldate = {2025-05-22},
  abstract = {Oregon is on an extraordinary path to transform the delivery of health care to improve health outcomes, quality of care, and reduce costs through implementation of a ``coordinated care model.'' To succeed, the coordinated care model relies on health information technology, including new systems for capturing, analyzing, and sharing information about patient care and new models of sharing care information among all members of care teams. Oregon reinvigorated its health information technology strategic plan shortly after launching the coordinated care model for its Medicaid population. With unexpected state funding, Oregon leveraged significant federal funding and embarked on a significant public/private partnership opportunity that led to statewide health information exchange of hospital event information, under the Emergency Department Information Exchange (EDIE). That unprecedented success enabled further technology opportunities, and Oregon continues on its path toward supporting the right technology infrastructure and tools necessary for success.},
