  abstract = {Definitely completing my PhD training. For my PhD education in Texas, I drove 2 h each way to classes from Midland to night school at Lubbock, 3--4 days a week. I was working a full time day job as an academic in Odessa. Driving home after I successfully defended my dissertation I was almost delirious thinking I would never have to do that again. Ever. Be nice to everyone, be patient, and relish the failures. My failures are instrumental in any of the accomplishments I've had thus far. A 31 min drive to work, listening to sports talk on the radio, opening 150 or so emails from predatory journals and drinking about four cups of coffee. I watched the 1980 US Hockey team (Miracle on Ice) beat the Soviet Union on an old Philco television when I was 15 years old. I remember how proud it made everyone in the USA and how much we needed a boost as a country. I think I have a unique skill in taking complex information and simplifying it in a way that is useable to rehabilitative clinicians. At present, I think I've most influenced the understanding of diagnostic accuracy. My heroes are those individuals who are service oriented, who do so in anonymity, and who sacrifice so that others can gain. I've {\dots}},
